[38;2;124;124;124m\mathbb{Q} \setminus \{0\}$ with $r^n = q$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mTake $q = 2$ and $n = 2$. We need $r \in \mathbb{Q}$ with $r^2 = 2$. But $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\sqrt{2} \notin \mathbb{Q}$. So $\mathbb{Q} \setminus \{0\}$ is NOT divisible.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince homomorphic images of divisible groups are divisible, and $\mathbb{Q} [0m
