[38;2;124;124;124minteger $n$, since $G$ is divisible, there exists $g' \in G$ with $ng' = g$. [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mThen $\phi(g')^n = \phi(ng') = \phi(g) = h$ (in multiplicative notation for [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$H$). So $H$ is divisible.[0m

